Task: Extend OrderStore tests for reservation fields + get() (Red, mostly)

Summary: Added assertions on status/reservationId/reservedQuantity round-tripping to
existing create tests, plus new get() tests (existing id -> Some(order), unknown id ->
None) for both inMemory and postgres. inMemory's tests passed immediately (Green
implementation already existed from the Phase 1 coupling). The Postgres tests, however,
were genuinely Red: get()'s SELECT query used skunk's varchar codec for the item/status
columns, but the orders table declares them as Postgres text — Skunk's column-alignment
check (comparing the query's asserted decoder types against the DB's actual described
row) rejected the mismatch with a ColumnAlignmentException. Fixed by switching both the
SELECT decoder and the INSERT's item parameter encoder from varchar to text, matching
the actual column type.

Files changed:
- modules/order-service/src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderStoreSuite.scala
- modules/order-service/src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderStorePostgresSuite.scala
